  "published": "2026-10-31T15:38:27.123Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "0.2.0: To and from sqlsim (Microsoft sqlsimtools). export sqlsim writes a DaffyTee recording as sqlsim's replay XML, for sqlsim and sqlsim Studio: every request as T-SQL, procedure calls with their declared types, transactions the application ran through its driver as BEGIN/COMMIT/ROLLBACK TRANSACTION, in files within sqlsim's limits. import sqlsim reads sqlsim's replay XML (an Extended Events capture) into a recording DaffyReplay runs: pooled connections and resets kept, and the report says first what an Extended Events capture cannot tell (transactions opened through the driver, errors raised while a statement ran, rows per statement); an imported batch is compared on its row total. Replay and comparison of DaffyTee recordings are unchanged. Binaries signed by TroBeeONE LLC.\n0.1.1: The binaries are now Authenticode-signed by TroBeeONE LLC. Decodes datetime values as DaffyTee 0.3.1 does, rounded to the millisecond as SQL Server shows them (.000, .003, .007), so --approximate writes them as literals SQL Server accepts. DaffyTee 0.3.0 and earlier decoded a datetime after 00:02:23 wrong unless the recording has raw bytes: inspect warns about procedure calls without raw bytes that hold such values, and run --approximate skips them rather than send the wrong time.\n0.1.0: First release. Replays DaffyTee (0.3.0 or later) recordings against a test SQL Server at recorded pace (with --speed), fast or serial; byte-exact from --raw recordings, with transaction descriptors patched and prepared-statement and cursor handles mapped; approximate T-SQL for procedure calls recorded without raw bytes. inspect, target, run, report and compare commands; report.json and a self-contained report.html. Tested with ADO.NET, EF Core, ODBC and JDBC workloads on SQL Server 2022 and 2025.",
